{
  "_readme": "Edit freely. `locales` drive per-country web searches (needs BRAVE_API_KEY); `sources` are seed pages whose links are scanned. A locale's `proxyEnv` names an env var holding an HTTP proxy URL you operate/rent in that country (e.g. CRAWL_PROXY_CN=http://user:pass@host:port) — used only for sites that can't be reached from your own network. `searxEngines` is only used with SEARXNG_URL: the engines to query for that country (they must be enabled on your SearXNG). With SearXNG each query uses one engine from `searxEngines` in rotation and falls back to the next if it returns nothing (scraped engines rate-limit quickly). `search.recencyDays` limits results to pages posted/updated in that many days (0 = no limit); `search.pagesPerQuery` is how many result pages to page through per query. A source can set `adapter` (a reader in crawler/adapters.js for structured calendars such as 80.lv), `linkPattern` (a regex: follow every link on the page whose URL matches, instead of only 3D-looking ones), `limit` (max links to follow) or `disabled` (a reason; the source is skipped). A locale or source can set `weight` (default 1): each round of the page budget takes that many pages from it, so weight 2 gets about twice the share of weight 1. The Americas and Europe are weighted 2 to balance the large Asian contest sites.",
